{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124450","id":4849433285,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABIQx6xQ","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124450","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124450.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124450.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124450","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124450/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124450/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124450/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/e657120ccf3bec2e94fe1d4f22c0a25083fdfa08","number":124450,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Store each `GDType` member once and share it with subtypes by pointer","user":{"login":"bjorn","id":531764,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMTc2NA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/531764?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjorn","html_url":"https://github.com/bjorn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjorn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjorn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjorn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjorn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjorn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjorn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjorn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjorn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bjorn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Introduction\r\n\r\nThis change builds on optimization work done by @Ivorforce in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122751. It's a nice change, and now that all member types are stored in a unified hash map, it becomes easy to save further memory by allocating each member only once and storing only pointers in the `_members` map.\r\n\r\nIn the first version of this patch I had every `GDType::Member` allocated separately on the heap, but this of course caused cache misses which slowed down property access a little. To avoid this, I kept the memory packed by using a `PagedAllocator<GDType::Member, true, 1024>` (locking enabled because these types can be added from multiple threads, my measurements indicate it was still faster than doing separate `memnew` allocations).\r\n\r\nI have tried to keep the patch focused on one thing, but due to the previous public exposure of the `AHashMap<StringName, Member>` storage there was a need to introduce some helper functions. At least all the necessary adjustments are very easy to review. That maybe should have gone into a separate commit and I can split it up on request. All the interesting bits are in `gdtype.h` and `gdtype.cpp`.\r\n\r\nDisclosure: While I have taken great care to understand the approach and to test and review the code, I have relied on different AI models during development, both for finding this solution and doing the necessary API changes.\r\n\r\nMeasured on an editor build (Ryzen 9 3950X, GCC 16.2), against befe24c831:\r\n- Static memory: 45.8 MB -> 32.0 MB (-30%). Process `VmData` drops by the same 13.8 MB.\r\n- Member lookups: +0.5% instructions (callgrind), no measurable change in cycles or cache misses (`perf stat`).\r\n- Type registration at startup (`--benchmark`, median of 20 runs): `[Scene] Register Types` 25.4 ms -> 21.6 ms.\r\n\r\nI've posted the full benchmarks at https://gist.github.com/bjorn/a8f9aff7e40ca35ed6f9101459f83131\r\n\r\n## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\nReduces static memory used by `GDType::Member` instances and speeds up type registration, while not meaningfully affecting access speed.\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\n`GDType::Member` gained two members:\r\n\r\n* `StringName name`: Since the `_self_members` of each class are now stored in a plain `LocalVector`, the names are no longer available from the keys of the `AHashMap`. Hence, when the own-members are iterated, their names now come from this member.\r\n\r\n* `const GDType *owner`: Since the only remaining `AHashMap<StringName, const Member *>` used to look up members by name is the one storing all members (including inherited ones), this owner pointer was added to enable member-only lookup to return `nullptr` when the owner does not match the current type in `get_member`.\r\n\r\n`GDType` gained one member:\r\n\r\n* `LocalVector<const GDType *> _type_hierarchy`: This member is not strictly necessary in this PR, but it simplified the `MemberRange` type since this way it can iterate either own-members only or all members in hierarchy order (starting from the root type) using one unified implementation. The `members(bool p_no_inheritance)` function would otherwise need to return a type that can iterate either a `LocalVector` or an `AHashMap` (but I also plan a follow-up PR that actually speeds up member access and reduces static memory usage further, which replaces the `AHashMap`).\r\n\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097966,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc5NjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:core","name":"topic:core","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"arc